Chapter 7 — Exact Algorithms

7.1 Backward Recursion for Finite-Horizon Viability

Algorithm 7.1. Given S, A, \mathcal{P}, \tilde{K}, H:

```
V_H := K̃
For t = H-1 down to 0:
    V_t := ∅
    For each s ∈ K̃:
        If ∃ a ∈ A(s) such that ∀ P ∈ P(s,a), P(V_{t+1} | s,a) = 1:
            V_t := V_t ∪ {s}
Return (V_0, ..., V_H)
```

Operation count: O(H \cdot |\tilde{K}| \cdot |A| \cdot |\mathcal{P}|).

7.2 Value Iteration for the Viability Kernel

Algorithm 7.2. Given S, A, \mathcal{P}, \tilde{K}:

```
V := K̃
Repeat:
    V' := T_P(V)
    If V' = V: break
    V := V'
Return V
```

Convergence: By Theorem 4.5, the sequence stabilizes in at most |S| steps.

7.3 Optimal Viable Policy

Algorithm 7.3. Given S, A, \mathcal{P}, \tilde{K}, \gamma, c, V_\infty:

```
Initialize V(s) := 0 for all s ∈ V_∞
Repeat:
    For each s ∈ V_∞:
        V'(s) := min_{a ∈ A_safe(s)} [ c(s,a) + γ sup_{P ∈ P(s,a)} Σ_{s'} P(s'|s,a) V(s') ]
    If max_s |V'(s) - V(s)| < ε: break
    V := V'
π*(s) := argmin over A_safe(s)
Return π*, V
```

Operation count: O(|V_\infty| \cdot |A| \cdot |\mathcal{P}| \cdot \log(1/\epsilon) / (1-\gamma)).

7.4 Pareto Frontier Computation

Algorithm 7.4 (Multi-objective VI with pruning). For each s, maintain a Pareto set V_t(s) \subseteq \mathbb{R}^3. The update is:

Q_t(s,a) = \left\{ c(s,a) + \gamma \sum_{s'} P(s' \mid s,a) v_{s'} : v_{s'} \in V_{t-1}(s'), P \in \mathcal{P}(s,a) \right\}

then prune by dominance.

Pruning complexity: O(P \log P) per state-action pair, where P = |V_t(s)|. Worst-case P can be exponential in H; limited-precision approaches yield tractable approximations.

