Appendix G — Three-Module Model Details

G.1 State Space Enumeration

The state space S is the disjoint union over topologies G \in \{G_0, G_1, G_2, G_3\} of

S_G = Z \times H(G) \times P_{\mathrm{conf}},

where

· Z = \{0,\dots,10\} \times \{0,\dots,5\} \times \{0,\dots,5\}, so |Z| = 11 \times 6 \times 6 = 396.
· H(G) = \{\mathsf{H}, \mathsf{D}, \mathsf{F}\}^{|V(G)|}, so |H(G)| = 3^{|V(G)|}.
· P_{\mathrm{conf}} is the set of pending modification configurations. With k_{\max} = 2 and four possible modification types, |P_{\mathrm{conf}}| = 1 + 4 \cdot 2 + \binom{4}{2} \cdot 2^2 = 1 + 8 + 24 = 33.

Thus

|S| = \sum_{G} 396 \cdot 3^{|V(G)|} \cdot 33.

For G_0, |V(G_0)| = 3, so |H(G_0)| = 27.
For G_1, |V(G_1)| = 4, so |H(G_1)| = 81.
For G_2, |V(G_2)| = 2, so |H(G_2)| = 9.
For G_3, |V(G_3)| = 3, so |H(G_3)| = 27.

Then

|S| = 396 \cdot 33 \cdot (27 + 81 + 9 + 27) = 396 \cdot 33 \cdot 144 = 1{,}881{,}792.

This is on the order of 10^6 states.

G.2 Transition Probability Specification

The nominal kernel P_0(w \mid s, a) is a product distribution over w = (d, f, \delta). We specify:

P_0(d \mid s, a) = \begin{cases}
0.5 & d = 0 \\
0.3 & d = 1 \\
0.2 & d = 2
\end{cases}

P_0(f \mid s, a) = \begin{cases}
0.95 & f = 0 \\
0.05 & f = 1
\end{cases}

P_0(\delta \mid s, a) = \begin{cases}
0.9 & \delta = 0 \\
0.1 & \delta = 1
\end{cases}

These probabilities are independent of s and a for simplicity. The ambiguity set is a total variation ball:

\mathcal{P}(s,a) = \left\{ P \in \Delta(W) : \|P - P_0(\cdot \mid s,a)\|_{\mathrm{TV}} \leq \rho \right\}.

The extreme points of this set can be enumerated by shifting probability mass to the least likely outcomes.

G.3 Failure Map

The failure map \phi_{\mathrm{fail}} selects a module uniformly at random from V_t when f_t = 1. If the selected module is healthy, it becomes failed. If no healthy module exists, no failure occurs.

